          "finalUrl": "https://www.ncl.ac.uk/who-we-are/our-campuses/newcastle-campus/helix/",
          "intro": "Logo Search for something Search... Search... Newcastle University Who We Are Our Campuses Newcastle Campus Newcastle Helix Newcastle Helix We are developing Newcastle Helix together with Newcastle City Council and Legal and General . Key aims The Helix fulfils three key functions for us: The site itself is a living laboratory . Projects and experiments run at scale, in real time. Infrastructure, urban planning, data, and ageing are themes of our research at Helix By locating alongside businesses, we close the gap between academic research and commercial innovation New buildings increase our capacity for research, education and engagement Landmark location The Newcastle Helix site is a landmark location. In total it comprises: 24 acres 20 different building plots 6 residential plots an estimated 4,000 jobs The site includes the following buildings: Newcastle Business School The Catalyst Urban Sciences Building Frederick Douglass Centre Contact us For further information about our work: Email: info@newcastlehelix.com Address: Newcastle Science Central Management LLP c/o Newcastle University 4th Floor, Kings Gate Newcastle upon Tyne NE1 7RU Links to other centres Centre for Ageing Centre for Data Energy Systems Integration",
