        "cityDefinitionNote": "City IDs are nearby settlements or rural visitor areas for filtering, not legal municipal-boundary claims. New viewports are centred on the first verified visit point in that locality, not asserted town centroids. Ambiguous names use newborough-anglesey, minffordd-cadair, pontarfynach, dundrum-ni and killaloo-ni. Northern Ireland sites do not reuse England's Newcastle city ID.",
        "methodology": [
          "Read current data/index.js referenced shards; do not treat orphan cells as active. Existing Wales/NI nature points Bute Park and Belfast Botanic Gardens were not duplicated.",
          "Primary visit evidence comes from the managing body, national park authority, NRW, NI government, local council, RSPB, WWT or official destination organisations.",
          "National Trust raw HTTP requests returned an HTTP 200 Radware browser challenge. That body was not accepted as verification. NT facts were read through the web tool's public primary-page index, including actual address, access and current opening tables.",
          "Where official location metadata identified a general area rather than an arrival facility, small OSM API bounding boxes were used to identify actual named visitor buildings, public parking or trail-information points. No Nominatim requests were made.",
          "NRW official grid references were used to anchor searches; final published points use the matching OSM geometry/POI. Three-figure NGR cells are 100 m references and were not falsely presented as precise entrances.",
          "OSM way positions are geometry bounds centres, not entrance nodes. OSM opening-hours tags and old operator/Forestry Commission labels were not used to establish current operating status.",
          "Feature points (Pistyll Rhaeadr, Devil's Bridge Falls, gardens and some park references) explicitly use pointRole feature-reference. All 53 entrance values are null.",
          "Coordinates are WGS84 references; numeric decimal precision is not a surveyed accuracy claim. No prices, walk duration or travel time are hard-coded.",
          "Country checks use managing-body address/country evidence and the verified mapped location. No Republic of Ireland nature sites or cross-border summit point is published."
        ],
